  "2026-10-26T22:26:14.014Z",codex-agent,"Full source-head gates passed at 0b9f2422b7e70e48c23a77cfd494e4b1043c0923: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40410497129 . npm on Node 22 and Node 26 plus Bun on Node 26 each passed 386 suite tests and four packed-acceptance results, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Coverage is 100/100/100/100 across 34 source files at unchanged thresholds and exclusions. Every command ran from npm and Bun tarballs in fresh non-Git consumers. Identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, changelog and attestation checks passed; CodeQL also passed. Earlier round-7 runs 40402171049 and 40409473196 failed compound-close handling and synthetic-query coverage respectively; they are not used as green evidence. Native settings registration, universal cold/provider write-free reads and atomic compound close remain unmet SDK capabilities, so PR 24 remains draft. Releasing this claim while retaining in_progress; an evidence-only commit will receive its own exact-head CI verification."
  "2026-10-26T23:15:19.925Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator scope split: native settings-section registration and its provider-aware reader move to pm-swarm-native-settings, blocked on unbraind/pm-cli#1580. This PR retains typed settings, matching flags, audited persistence and the documented compatibility reader. The acceptance text now excludes native registration. Correcting the earlier close-gap assessment: public commitItemMutations builds update and close steps on commitWorkspaceTransaction; implement and prove durable recovery here, then close pm-swarm-atomic-close under the explicit orchestrator instruction."
  "2026-10-26T23:25:53.932Z",codex-agent,"Public SDK transaction correction: atomic close is supported. Implemented commitItemMutations over commitWorkspaceTransaction with deterministic deriveMutationTransactionId, guarded update/unset then native close, an owned recovery receipt and native compensation. New close suite passes 25/25; three isolated behavioral reversions produce 16 expected failing results, documented on pm-swarm-atomic-close. The SDK pin remains unchanged. Merged origin/main, including the toolchain update, without tracker conflicts; npm and coverage runners now explicitly use at most two workers. Native settings registration is split to pm-swarm-native-settings, blocked on upstream #1580, rather than a draft criterion."
  "2026-10-26T23:31:03.241Z",codex-agent,"Restored pinned-PM checks pass: close recovery 25/25, existing compound-write checks 2/2, writer inventory/source matrix 7/7 and whole-document matrix 22/22. Typecheck, lint, 150 documented declarations across 35 authored files, zero duplication, identity and changelog checks pass. Local strict health is limited by an unrelated globally discovered pm-github extension version skew (host 2026.10.23 versus extension 2026.10.26); no global extension or SDK pin was changed. The isolated CI strict-health and full npm/Bun gates remain required before completion."
  "2026-10-26T23:36:31.529Z",codex-agent,"Final close changes are ready for CI: canonical identity and token handling are inside the operation lease; 26 recovery tests and 11 fencing tests pass, with four behavioral revert probes producing 17 expected failures. Native registration remains solely in the blocked #1580 follow-up. The PR will be marked ready with current-head gates pending, then the explicitly authorized atomic-close item will be closed after full CI evidence."
  "2026-10-26T23:52:19.464Z",codex-agent,CI run 40420946048 identified two retained refusal regressions in the close refactor; both are corrected and the restored targeted suite passes 33/33. Pure local SDK inspection precedes usage-producing reads and the fresh host snapshot is still checked under the lease and native item lock. Malformed stored fences retain the repair diagnostic. Six behavioral revert probes now produce 19 expected failures. No thresholds or SDK pins changed. Current-head full CI must be rerun.
  "2026-10-27T00:31:20.943Z",codex-agent,"Current source-head full gates passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40424027439 at e1286a3056eb8ac17d0551c052bb46e6c6cdae85. npm Node 22, npm Node 26 and Bun Node 26 each pass 414 suite and four packed-acceptance results; 100/100/100/100 coverage across 35 sources; zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Runners use at most two workers. Isolated strict health, identity, types, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, audit, packing, changelog and attestation pass. Atomic-close is implemented and explicitly closed; native settings registration is outside this acceptance scope in pm-swarm-native-settings, blocked on #1580 with sdk-gap and upstream tags. origin/main is merged, PR 24 is ready. Releasing this claim while retaining in_progress. The final tracking-only commit will receive exact-head CI."
